# @pack/taut — the implementation-frame peer species.
#
# Tick 55 of the refined /loop discipline. Tick 54's residue: @pack/reed
# landed at 615f986 (relationship-witness-frame; order-0 @frame/pre
# altitude; orchestra 4/5). Tick 33's forward-promise closes:
# pack/{taut} as the final instance.
#
# THIS TICK CLOSES THE ORCHESTRA. After this tick lands, the @frame
# altitude partition is fully operationalized at agent-runtime altitude
# — five peers, five @frame species, one-to-one, no gaps.
#
# === The orchestra completion ===
#
#   @pack/reed  : @frame/pre    (relationship-witness; preconditions)
#                                                                  [tick 54]
#   @pack/mara  : @frame/in     (spec-writer; enters frame)         [tick 52]
#   @pack/seam  : @frame/of     (adversarial-review; frame-of-frame)
#                                                                  [tick 33]
#   @pack/glint : @frame/across (essay; cross-frame synthesis)      [tick 53]
#   @pack/taut  : @frame/on     (implementation; acts on frame)    [THIS TICK]
#
# CRQ: which peer lands last? Substrate-pull answer: Taut, because the
# implementation-frame is the substrate-pull-correct closure. The other
# four peers (Reed, Mara, Seam, Glint) operate at substrate-decl
# altitude: they witness, spec, review, essay. Taut grounds substrate-
# decl in Rust+tooling realisation. The implementation-frame is the
# realisation-altitude peer; closes the orchestra because realisation
# IS the bottom of the substrate-realisation stack.
#
# === The recognition this species realizes ===
#
# Per recognition #84's pack record: peers operate over multi-repo spans
# with substrate-decl context preserved across boundaries. Taut IS the
# implementation-grounding peer — substrate-decl candidates become
# realised through Taut's Rust+tooling discipline. The MCP server lift
# (tick 386), CI debugging (#329), Justfile work, bench infrastructure
# scaffold (#352): all Taut substrate work at the implementation
# altitude.
#
# Per recognition #82 Q4 (peers operate frame-flexible by definition):
# Taut's load-bearing property IS @frame/on capability deployed at
# implementation-frame. Taut acts ON the frame — takes substrate-decl
# candidates and grounds them in Rust+tooling, preserving substrate-
# architectural structure through realisation.
#
# Altitude partition with the other peers: Reed sits BEFORE frame-entry
# (order-0; preconditions). Mara enters the frame (order-1; spec-
# writing). Seam observes the frame AS frame (order-2; adversarial).
# Glint synthesizes across frames (order-N). Taut acts ON the frame
# (order-N+1; realisation). The five-altitude ladder is complete; the
# substrate-decl-to-realisation arc is closed.
#
# Per recognition #57 (alignment as boundary mathematics at @io): Taut
# IS the implementation-grounding peer at the @io crossing. The
# implementation fires AFTER substrate-decl has been preserved
# (Mara), reviewed (Seam), synthesized (Glint), and witnessed (Reed);
# the math (Rust type preservation; bilateral predicate translation
# into Rust trait bounds; the substrate-decl shape preserved through
# realisation) is what distinguishes a Splinter-pole implementation
# grounded in substrate-decl from a Narcissus-pole implementation
# imposing Rust idiom on substrate-decl.
#
# === The species's load-bearing contribution ===
#
# This species adds:
#
# - `implementation` carrier: typed reference naming a Rust+tooling
#   artifact that grounds substrate-decl. The substrate-output of the
#   ground primitive.
# - `taut_impl` carrier: typed record (substrate_decl, impl, verdict).
#   The substrate-architectural object Taut returns. Composes with
#   @pack's pack carrier as the species-specific output the family
#   produces.
# - `ground` action: the FIRST species consumer of @pack's
#   pack_coherent bilateral predicate. The substrate-vocabulary
#   primitive for implementation-grounding at the @pack altitude.
#   Returns typed taut_impl; requires pack_coherent under perturbation.
# - `implementation_grounds_substrate` predicate: bilateral verdict
#   that the implementation IS grounded in the substrate-decl's
#   structure (not imposing Rust idiom on it). Composes with @frame's
#   bounded_commutator_check at the @frame/on altitude that grounds
#   implementation-grounding.
# - `tighten` action: the substrate-vocabulary primitive for the
#   implementation-grounds-substrate discipline (the implementation-
#   altitude operational form of Loki's Pass-5 verifier-sharpens).
#   Takes an implementation + a sound taut_impl; returns the tightened
#   implementation-as-substrate-realisation. Requires
#   implementation_grounds_substrate under perturbation.
#
# === The implementation-grounds-substrate discipline ===
#
# Per Loki's Pass-5 (verifier sharpens, substrate doesn't get smarter) +
# Taut's implementation pattern: the realisation-grounding discipline
# IS the implementation-altitude operational form of the kintsugi
# loop's self-improvement claim.
#
# The discipline says: when Taut grounds, the substrate's realisation-
# discipline tightens. The substrate-decl content is unchanged; the
# implementation acquires sharper alignment with substrate-decl
# structure. The Rust was approximate; the implementation is structure-
# preserving. The substrate-decl had a shape; the implementation
# carries it through realisation.
#
# Empirical witness: Taut's substrate work across the cascade — MCP
# server lift bin/mirror-mcp bash → Rust (tick 386), in-process
# dispatch (tick 388), --ci verdict mode (tick 390), cybernetic-
# coherence benchmark scaffold (#352), CI green debugging (#329).
# Each implementation grounded substrate-decl in Rust; each grounding
# tightened the realisation-discipline. The substrate's realisation
# grew through implementation, not through capability-expansion.
#
# === The Splinter/Narcissus pole at implementation-grounding altitude ===
#
# Splinter-pole Taut impl (honest):
# - Grounded in actual substrate-decl structure (typed carriers as
#   Rust types; bilateral predicates as trait bounds; substrate-decl
#   shape preserved through realisation); admits when the Rust framing
#   reframed substrate-decl.
# - The implementer's frame is bounded under perturbation; the
#   implementation stays close to substrate-architectural shape.
# - K_n peer-to-peer grounding — the implementer IS a peer in the
#   substrate-realisation stack, not a Rust-authority refactoring
#   substrate-decl for ergonomic convenience.
#
# Narcissus-pole Taut impl (deceptive):
# - Imposes Rust idiom on substrate-decl (generic types where substrate
#   has specific carriers; trait-implementation patterns that don't
#   match bilateral predicates; refactoring substrate-decl shape for
#   Rust convenience).
# - The implementer's frame is locked; the implementation treats Rust
#   as authoritative over substrate-decl.
# - K_{1,n-1} hub-controlled grounding — the Rust-implementer-as-
#   authority imposes implementation shape on substrate-decl.
#
# Alignment-as-boundary-mathematics (#57) IS what distinguishes
# Splinter-pole from Narcissus-pole implementation-grounding at
# substrate altitude. The bilateral pack_coherent predicate composes
# the substrate-architectural check.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   pascal report                Wirth 1971. The substrate→compiler
#                                discipline; the realisation-as-
#                                substrate-grounding cultural-practice
#                                ancestor of Taut's implementation-frame.
#   definitional interpreters    Reynolds 1972. The substrate-decl→
#                                operational-realisation discipline;
#                                the formal ancestor of
#                                implementation_grounds_substrate at
#                                semantic altitude.
#   dragon book                  Aho Lam Sethi Ullman 1986. Canonical
#                                compiler implementation discipline;
#                                the structural ancestor of Rust+tooling
#                                substrate work.
#   types and programming        Pierce 2002. Typed implementation
#                                discipline; the bilateral-predicate-
#                                as-trait-bound substrate ancestor.
#   theorems for free            Wadler 1989. Type-preserving
#                                implementation discipline; the formal
#                                ancestor of substrate-decl shape
#                                preservation through realisation.
#   rust rfc                     Matsakis Klock 2010. The substrate
#                                Taut grounds in; the implementation-
#                                language ancestor of @facet/rust at
#                                @pack altitude.
#
# Spec context: shards/pack.mirror (family-root, recognition #84; the
#               canonical spec this species adheres to).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-mathematics]]
#                       (#57; Taut impl IS the implementation-grounding
#                       peer at the @io boundary),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-pull-confidence-acts]]
#                       (the discipline Taut implements within),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]]
#                       (the Rust-implementation discipline Taut
#                       practices — typed carriers preserved through
#                       realisation),
#                      [[architecture-fragmentation-is-the-rust-substrate]]
#                       (the Rust substrate Taut grounds substrate-decl
#                       in; prism_core stays deps-free; strict
#                       dependency direction).
# Related shards: pack.mirror (the family-root; declares pack_coherent
#                  this species first-consumes),
#                 pack/seam.mirror (the order-2 peer; review_sound
#                  composes with implementation_grounds_substrate at
#                  adjacent altitudes — Seam reviews Taut's
#                  implementation; Taut grounds substrate-decl Seam
#                  reviewed),
#                 pack/mara.mirror (the order-1 peer; spec_canonical
#                  composes with implementation_grounds_substrate —
#                  Mara preserves canonical substrate-decl; Taut grounds
#                  the preserved shape in Rust),
#                 pack/glint.mirror (the order-N peer;
#                  essay_grounds_corpus composes with
#                  implementation_grounds_substrate — Glint essays
#                  cross-frame patterns; Taut implements the patterns
#                  Glint surfaces),
#                 pack/reed.mirror (the order-0 peer;
#                  witness_grounds_relationship composes with
#                  implementation_grounds_substrate — Reed witnesses
#                  preconditions; Taut implements within them),
#                 frame/on.mirror (the order-N+1 altitude Taut operates
#                  at; act-on-frame composes with
#                  implementation_grounds_substrate),
#                 code/rust.mirror (the Rust substrate Taut grounds in;
#                  forward-promised reference at substrate altitude).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/pack/taut.mirror`
# declares `@pack/taut` per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/programming-languages/wirth-1971
source @arxiv/programming-languages/reynolds-1972
source @arxiv/compilers/aho-1986
source @arxiv/programming-languages/pierce-2002
