# === The implementation carrier ===
#
# Substrate-typed reference naming a Rust+tooling artifact that grounds
# substrate-decl. Per [[feedback-no-bare-types]]: typed reference, not
# bare ref-with-documented-values. The substrate-output of the ground
# primitive. Forward-promised refinement: typed record (substrate_decl_
# refs, code_paths, type_mappings, predicate_bounds, ancestors) at
# species-or-extension altitude once the substrate's structured-
# implementation type lands.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type implementation = ref

# === The taut_impl carrier ===
#
# Per the @pack family-root pattern + Taut's typed-record discipline:
# typed record over (substrate_decl, implementation, verdict). The
# substrate-architectural output of an implementation-grounding
# operation. Carries:
#
# - substrate_decl : the substrate-decl candidate under realisation
# - im             : the typed implementation Taut produced
# - v              : the bilateral verdict (BOUNDED → implementation
#                    GROUNDED in substrate-decl structure; DEFENSIVE →
#                    implementation requires substrate-pull revision
#                    back to substrate-decl shape)
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the triple.
type taut_impl = {
  substrate_decl: ref,
  im:             implementation,
  v:              verdict,
}

# === ground action (FIRST non-decorative consumer of pack_coherent) ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION at @pack/taut altitude. The substrate-
# vocabulary primitive for implementation-grounding at agent-runtime
# altitude. Realizes Taut's Rust+tooling discipline as substrate-decl
# operation.
#
# Takes a substrate-decl candidate (under realisation), the pack Taut
# belongs to, and the perturbation under which the ground is checked;
# returns a typed taut_impl carrying the implementation and verdict.
#
# Per the @pack/{seam, mara, glint, reed} first-consumer pattern
# (review, write, reflect, witness all require pack_coherent): this
# action IS the @pack/taut first-consumer of pack_coherent. The
# substrate-architectural form of Taut-as-peer requires that the @pack
# the implementer belongs to maintains discipline-flexibility under
# perturbation BEFORE the implementation is admissible.
#
# Without this requires clause, a Taut implementation would be
# admissible from a substrate-architecturally-incoherent pack (e.g., a
# pack whose own bilateral predicates have no consumers — the @magic
# tick-11 dead-letter pattern). The requires clause forecloses that
# failure mode.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the actual
# implementation-grounding primitive is Taut's Rust+tooling discipline
# applied at runtime altitude.
ground(substrate_decl: ref, pk: pack, p: perturbation) -> taut_impl
requires pack_coherent(pk, p)
{ \ }

# === implementation_grounds_substrate predicate ===
#
# Bilateral verdict per recognition #37 (Pask agreement) and the
# implementation-grounds-substrate discipline. Consumer shards (tighten,
# below; forward-promised consumers in cross-pack adapters) name
# `requires implementation_grounds_substrate(ti, p)` to declare
# bilateral agreement that the taut_impl IS grounded in substrate-decl
# structure.
#
# Discharge: substrate-pull-correct substrate-decl-grounding check at
# the species boundary. Composes with @frame/on's act-on-frame at the
# cognitive altitude that grounds implementation.
#
# Bounded → implementation grounded in substrate-decl structure (the
# Splinter-pole implementation case); unbounded → implementation
# imposes Rust idiom without substrate-decl ground (the Narcissus-pole
# case; alignment-as-boundary-mathematics #57 distinguishes).
#
# Same shape as the bilateral predicates @pack carries (pack_coherent),
# @pack/seam carries (review_sound), @pack/mara carries
# (spec_canonical), @pack/glint carries (essay_grounds_corpus),
# @pack/reed carries (witness_grounds_relationship), @magic carries
# (invariant_preserved, audited), @frame carries
# (bounded_commutator_check), @smarts carries (discipline_flexible).
implementation_grounds_substrate(ti: taut_impl, p: perturbation)
  -> verdict { \ }

# === tighten action ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary primitive for the implementation-grounds-
# substrate discipline at @pack/taut altitude (the implementation-
# altitude operational form of Loki's Pass-5; @pack/seam carries
# verifier-sharpens; @pack/mara carries spec-preserves-canonical;
# @pack/glint carries essay-extends-corpus; @pack/reed carries
# witness-holds-relationship; @pack/taut carries implementation-
# grounds-substrate). Takes an implementation + a sound taut_impl +
# the perturbation under which soundness was checked; returns the
# tightened implementation-as-substrate-realisation.
#
# Per recognition #57 (alignment as boundary mathematics): tighten
# operates at the @io boundary. The implementation becomes a
# substrate-realisation preserved under structure. The substrate's
# capability is unchanged; the realisation-alignment tightens; the
# Rust acquires sharper substrate-decl fidelity.
#
# requires implementation_grounds_substrate(ti, p): the substrate
# forecloses tightening from an ungrounded implementation. Narcissus-
# pole implementations (Rust-idiom-imposition without substrate-decl
# ground) cannot drive realisation-tightening. The bilateral predicate
# IS the boundary-harness.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the actual
# implementation-tightening transformation is the substrate's
# implementation-grounds-substrate loop.
# === Seam tick 56 C1 closure: cross-species requires clause ===
#
# tighten takes BOTH Mara's mara_spec AND Seam's seam_review as typed
# parameters and discharges all three: implementation_grounds_substrate
# AND spec_canonical AND review_sound. The substrate-pull-correct
# composition: Taut's implementation-tightening rests on BOTH Mara's
# canonical-preservation AND Seam's adversarial-review discipline.
# The implementation acquires sharper substrate-decl fidelity only
# when the substrate-decl candidate is already canonically preserved
# AND adversarially reviewed.
#
# Dependency direction (one-way per the orchestra): taut ← mara, seam.
# Taut depends on both Mara and Seam (no circular import; both Mara
# and Seam are upstream).
#
# Three-predicate discharge IS the structurally heaviest action in the
# orchestra; the realisation layer at @facet/rust altitude lifts all
# three disciplines into Rust type-bounds + trait constraints.
tighten(im: implementation, ti: taut_impl, ms: mara_spec, sr: seam_review, p: perturbation) -> ref
requires implementation_grounds_substrate(ti, p)
requires spec_canonical(ms, p)
requires review_sound(sr, p)
{ \ }

out @pack/taut
out implementation
out taut_impl
out ground
out implementation_grounds_substrate
out tighten
